            "content": "# Plan: Fix Background Download + Slow Gallery Entry\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\nBoth problems share the same root cause: iOS detects that camera Wi-Fi has no internet access.\n\n### Problem 1: Lock screen stops download after ~60s\n- iOS sees camera Wi-Fi has no internet → on lock screen, may deprioritize/disconnect Wi-Fi\n- Without cellular coexistence, system may route all traffic attempts through the dead Wi-Fi\n\n### Problem 2: Gallery entry takes 15s after Wi-Fi connected\n- After NEHotspotConfiguration.apply succeeds, iOS performs captive network detection (~15s)\n- During this time, `NEHotspotNetwork.fetchCurrent` returns nil (Wi-Fi not \"ready\")\n- The polling loop waits until iOS finishes captive detection\n\n## Solution: Allow Cellular Coexistence (XApp behavior)\n\nXApp's approach: when connecting to camera Wi-Fi, iOS shows \"this Wi-Fi has no internet, use cellular data?\" prompt. User allows → cellular stays active for internet, camera Wi-Fi stays for PTP.\n\n### Implementation\n\n1. **Set `NEHotspotConfiguration.allowCellular = true`** (iOS 17+) — this tells iOS to keep cellular active alongside camera Wi-Fi. This should:\n   - Eliminate the captive detection delay (cellular provides internet validation)\n   - Keep Wi-Fi stable during lock screen (system doesn't need to switch back for internet)\n\n2. **If `allowCellular` isn't available or insufficient**: Use `IP_BOUND_IF` on the PTP socket BUT only bind AFTER confirming Wi-Fi is connected to camera (when we get a valid 192.168.0.x address on en0). The previous attempt failed because binding was unconditional.\n\n3. **Remove the polling loop for Wi-Fi readiness**: Instead of polling `fetchCurrentSSID` every 500ms for 15 seconds, detect Wi-Fi readiness by attempting PTP connect directly to 192.168.0.1 — if the socket connects, Wi-Fi is ready regardless of what iOS captive detection thinks.\n\n## Steps\n\n- [ ] Check if NEHotspotConfiguration has allowCellular or equivalent on